    intro: "Asking is just the same little sentences with two new tools: a question word where the answer would go, and か at the end. おくには どちらですか asks 'where are you from?'; おしごとは なんですか asks 'what do you do?'. Then two small glue words do a lot of work — の, to say where you belong (a student of Sakura University), and も, to say 'me too'. And a country name plus 〜じん makes a nationality: イギリス becomes イギリスじん.",
