        nameJa: "どうしの ていねいな かたち",
        meaning: "polite verb: do / don't / did / didn't",
        explanation: "Four polite endings on the same verb. たべます (eat / will eat), たべません (don't eat), たべました (ate), たべませんでした (didn't eat). The plain 〜ます form covers both present and future — あした はたらきます is 'I'll work tomorrow'. For a question, just add か: たべますか. The time word usually comes near the front, with its に.",
        watchFor: "To answer 'no, I didn't', reach for 〜ませんでした, the longest one.",
